---
import { lines, payments, offers, tags, suppliers } from './facts.mjs';
const { kind, number, title } = Astro.props;
---
<figure class="model-figure" aria-label={title}>
  <figcaption><span>Figure {number}</span> {title}</figcaption>
  <div class="drawing">
    {kind === 'grain' && <>
      <div class="two">
        <div><h4>Order 101 · two lines</h4>{lines.filter(l=>l.order===101).map(l=><p class="record">Line {l.line} · {l.product} × {l.quantity}<br/><small>Agreed price {l.price}</small></p>)}</div>
        <div><h4>Order 101 · two payments</h4>{payments.map(p=><p class="record">Payment {p.id} · {p.amount}<br/><small>{p.method}</small></p>)}</div>
      </div>
      <p class="direction">↓ Put each line beside each payment ↓</p>
      <div class="region" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Four combinations of lines and payments"><table><thead><tr><th>Line</th><th>Product</th><th>Payment</th><th>Amount</th></tr></thead><tbody>{lines.filter(l=>l.order===101).flatMap(l=>payments.map(p=><tr><td>{l.line}</td><td>{l.product}</td><td>{p.id}</td><td>{p.amount}</td></tr>))}</tbody></table></div>
      <p class="verdict">Four rows, still only two payments.<br/>Nothing says which payment paid for which line.</p>
    </>}
    {kind === 'relationships' && <>
      <div class="relation"><div class="record"><b>customers</b><br/><small>PK customer_id</small></div><p>One customer per order<br/><strong>1 ← 0…many</strong><br/>Zero or more orders per customer</p><div class="record"><b>orders</b><br/><small>PK order_id<br/>FK customer_id · required</small></div></div>
      <div class="relation"><div class="record"><b>orders</b><br/><small>PK order_id</small></div><p>One order per line<br/><strong>1 ← 0…many</strong><br/>Zero or more lines per order*</p><div class="record"><b>order_items</b><br/><small>PK order_id + line_no<br/>FK product_id · required<br/>quantity · unit_price</small></div></div>
      <div class="relation"><div class="record"><b>products</b><br/><small>PK product_id</small></div><p>One product per line<br/><strong>1 ← 0…many</strong><br/>Zero or more lines per product</p><div class="record"><b>order_items</b><br/><small>A product can occur again<br/>on another line</small></div></div>
      <p class="foot">PK = primary key; FK = foreign key. *The reference permits an order with no lines. Requiring a submitted order to have a line is another rule.</p>
    </>}
    {kind === 'offers' && <>
      <h4>Actual offers · keep all three columns</h4>
      <div class="region" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Actual supplier product location offers"><table><thead><tr><th>Supplier</th><th>Product</th><th>Location</th></tr></thead><tbody>{offers.map(o=><tr>{o.map(x=><td>{x}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
      <p class="direction">↓ Each pair below exists somewhere above ↓</p>
      <div class="pairs"><p class="record">S1 ↔ P7<br/><small>from the first offer</small></p><p class="record">S1 ↔ South<br/><small>from the second offer</small></p><p class="record">P7 ↔ South<br/><small>from the third offer</small></p></div>
      <p class="verdict">S1 · P7 · South<br/><small>All three pairs fit. This offer was never made.</small></p>
    </>}
    {kind === 'split' && <>
      <h4>Original associations</h4>
      <div class="two"><p class="record">Order 101 → line 1 → P3</p><p class="record">Order 103 → line 1 → P7</p></div>
      <p class="direction">↓ Discard order_id from the product side ↓</p>
      <div class="two"><div class="record"><b>Order and line</b><p>101 · 1<br/>103 · 1</p></div><div class="record"><b>Line and product</b><p>1 · P3<br/>1 · P7</p></div></div>
      <p class="direction">↓ Match on line 1 ↓</p>
      <div class="region" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Reconstructed associations after an unsafe split"><table><thead><tr><th>Order</th><th>Line</th><th>Product</th><th>Was it there?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>101</td><td>1</td><td>P3</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr class="invented"><td>101</td><td>1</td><td>P7</td><td>Invented</td></tr><tr class="invented"><td>103</td><td>1</td><td>P3</td><td>Invented</td></tr><tr><td>103</td><td>1</td><td>P7</td><td>Yes</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      <p class="foot">Line 1 is unique within an order. Once the product side loses the order, the correct pairing is gone.</p>
    </>}
    {kind === 'independent' && <>
      <h4>P7 · two tags and two suppliers</h4>
      <div class="region" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Independent tags and suppliers combined"><table><thead><tr><th>Product</th><th>Tag</th><th>Supplier</th></tr></thead><tbody>{tags.flatMap(t=>suppliers.map(s=><tr><td>P7</td><td>{t}</td><td>{s}</td></tr>))}</tbody></table></div>
      <p class="direction">↓ Keep each independent set on its own ↓</p>
      <div class="two"><div class="record"><b>product_tags</b><p>P7 · gift<br/>P7 · ceramic</p></div><div class="record"><b>product_suppliers</b><p>P7 · S1<br/>P7 · S2</p></div></div>
      <p class="foot">A new tag needs one new product_tags row. It does not need one row for every supplier.</p>
    </>}
    {kind === 'price' && <>
      <div class="two"><div><h4>When order 103 is placed</h4><p class="record">products · P7<br/><b>price 20.00</b></p><p class="record">order_items · 103 / 1<br/><b>unit_price 20.00</b></p></div><div><h4>After the catalogue change</h4><p class="record">products · P7<br/><b>price 22.00</b><br/><small>Changed</small></p><p class="record">order_items · 103 / 1<br/><b>unit_price 20.00</b><br/><small>Still the agreed price</small></p></div></div>
      <p class="verdict">Order 103: (1 × 20.00) + (2 × 4.50) = 29.00</p>
      <p class="foot">The two prices answer different questions. Repricing the catalogue does not reprice an existing order.</p>
    </>}
  </div>
</figure>
<style>
.model-figure { margin:2.5rem 0; font-family:var(--font-sans); }
figcaption { margin-bottom:.75rem; font:500 1.06rem/1.5 var(--font-serif); }
figcaption span { font: .67rem/1.5 var(--font-sans); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.1em; margin-right:.7rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
.drawing { border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); padding:1.1rem; background:var(--color-surface); font:.86rem/1.6 var(--font-sans); }
h4 { font:500 .9rem/1.5 var(--font-sans); margin:0 0 .7rem; }
p { font:inherit; margin:.65rem 0; }
.two { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:1rem; }
.record { border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); background:var(--color-surface-alt); padding:.65rem .8rem; margin:0 0 .6rem; }
small { color:var(--color-text-secondary); font-size:.78rem; }
.direction { text-align:center; color:var(--color-text-secondary); margin:1rem 0; }
.verdict { border-left:3px solid var(--teal); padding:.65rem .85rem; margin:1rem 0 0; }
.foot { font-size:.78rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); margin:.9rem 0 0; }
.region { overflow-x:auto; }
.region:focus-visible { outline:2px solid var(--teal); outline-offset:3px; }
table { display:table; width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; font:inherit; margin:0; }
th,td { text-align:left; padding:.5rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule); white-space:nowrap; }
.invented { background:var(--color-surface-alt); font-weight:600; }
.pairs { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); gap:.6rem; }
.relation { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1.15fr 1fr; gap:.65rem; align-items:center; margin-bottom:1.1rem; }
.relation p { text-align:center; font-size:.74rem; }
.relation strong { display:block; font-size:1rem; color:var(--teal); }
.relation .record { text-align:left; }
@media(max-width:550px) { .two,.pairs { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:.5rem; } .relation { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:0; } .drawing {padding:.8rem;} .relation p { margin:.4rem 0; } }
</style>
